  "caption": "Quinn discovered Hyrox and trained everything, every day. By station 6 the technique had gone missing, and the knees and back filed a complaint.\n\nHyrox mixes running with tiring loaded stations, and fatigue can wear down technique — so knees, low back, Achilles, shoulders and hip flexors take extra strain. Hyrox itself isn't the problem; unprepared load often is.\n\nWhat can help: build running volume gradually, rehearse stations under fatigue in stages, strength-train the race positions, deal with niggles early, and taper for 7–10 days before race day.\n\nGet it checked if you have sharp pain on one side, pain at night, or pain lasting more than 4–5 days.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
